# ─── Google Sign-In OAuth Client IDs ─────────────────────────────────────────
# To enable Google sign-in:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ → APIs & Services → Credentials
# 2. Create OAuth 2.0 Client IDs for each platform:
#    - Web application (for Expo web and as fallback)
#    - iOS (bundle ID: from Xcode or Expo)
#    - Android (package name: from app.json or android/app/build.gradle)
# 3. For Android: add your SHA-1 fingerprint from `cd android && ./gradlew signingReport`
# 4. Restart the Expo bundler after changing these values
#
# NOTE: Leaving these EMPTY will cause the Google sign-in buttons to appear disabled.
# NOTE: Gemini AI also requires the "Generative Language API" to be enabled in GCP.
#
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=956886937569-s0db9qdqbkrgvpid8tv6179h17260bi5.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=956886937569-6gmg8ffsql5r4ppvupu9ommmqk89k9qo.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=956886937569-ksa8cldm1ootk02el858b63jmk50c6if.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ─── Emulator Host (DEV only) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
